---
import Base from '@layouts/Base.astro';
import Quiz from '@components/Quiz.astro';
import Gloss from '@components/Gloss.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Kaspa in 60 seconds — KasStacker"
  description="What Kaspa is, why it's fast, and why for years it could only move money — the one-minute foundation for everything else."
>
  <div class="wrap-narrow prose">
    <header class="head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Learn · stop 1 of 6</p>
      <h1>Kaspa in 60 seconds</h1>
    </header>

    <p><strong>Kaspa is digital cash secured by proof of work, like Bitcoin — but built to be fast.</strong></p>

    <p>
      Most blockchains make one block at a time and throw away ties. Kaspa keeps every block and weaves
      them into a <strong><Gloss term="blockdag">blockDAG</Gloss></strong> — a braid instead of a single chain — ordered by a protocol
      called <strong><Gloss term="ghostdag">GHOSTDAG</Gloss></strong>. The practical result: blocks arrive many times per second and
      payments confirm in seconds, while keeping Bitcoin-style proof-of-work security.
    </p>

    <blockquote>
      A chain is a single-lane road; a blockDAG is a motorway where every lane's traffic still ends up
      in one agreed order.
    </blockquote>

    <h2>The catch — until 2026</h2>
    <p>
      For years Kaspa's scripting was deliberately minimal. It could verify <em>who</em> owns coins and
      move them, but it couldn't enforce <em>conditions</em> on how coins move next. No vaults, no
      chain-enforced tokens, no on-chain agreements — money only.
    </p>
    <p>
      That is what the <strong>Toccata upgrade</strong> changed, and it's why this site exists.
    </p>

    <Quiz page="kaspa-in-60-seconds" />

    <div class="next-link"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/learn/what-toccata-changed">Next: What Toccata changed →</a></div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .head { padding: 56px 0 16px; }
  .head h1 { font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 700; margin-top: 8px; }
</style>
